# Prefer shadcn Components

Use **shadcn/ui** components from `@/components/ui/` instead of building equivalent UI from scratch. This keeps the design system consistent and reduces custom code.

## Rules

- **Before adding custom UI**: Check if a shadcn component exists (Button, Card, Dialog, DropdownMenu, Tooltip, Input, etc.). Use `npx shadcn@latest add <component>` if the component is not yet in the project.
- **Compose with shadcn**: Build features by composing shadcn components and styling with `className` / variants. Don’t reimplement buttons, modals, tooltips, or form controls with raw HTML + Tailwind.
- **When no shadcn fit**: If no shadcn component matches (e.g. a one-off illustration or layout), build a custom component and keep it in `components/` as per project structure.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom button/tooltip from scratch
<button className="rounded bg-blue-500 px-4 py-2 text-white hover:bg-blue-600">
  Submit
</button>
<span title="Help text">?</span>

// ✅ GOOD — use shadcn
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Tooltip, TooltipContent, TooltipTrigger } from "@/components/ui/tooltip";
<Button>Submit</Button>
<Tooltip>
  <TooltipTrigger asChild><Button variant="ghost" size="icon">?</Button></TooltipTrigger>
  <TooltipContent>Help text</TooltipContent>
</Tooltip>
```

- Need a dialog, dropdown, or popover? Add and use the shadcn component first instead of building a custom one.
